{{Term/Store|Spring of Wisdom||Series, BotW, TotK, AoC}} is a recurring location in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref>{{Cite|'''Spring of Wisdom'''|Map|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|'''Spring of Wisdom'''|Map|TotK}}</ref><ref name="Gallery">{{Cite|Here sits the Spring of Wisdom, wreathed in an aura of mystical energy. Make an offering here with a humble heart and your hands clasped in prayer.|Gallery (Interface)|AoC}}</ref>

==Features and Overview==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Quests|
{{BotW Quest
 |name= The Spring of Wisdom
 |type= Shrine Quest
 |giver= [[Medda]]
 |location= [[Hateno Village]]
}}
}}
The Spring of Wisdom is an [[Ancient Hylian Ruin]] located at the peak of [[Mount Lanayru]].<ref>{{Cite Book|quote= |book= CaC |publisher= |page= 413}}</ref> A pathway up Mount Lanayru leads travelers directly to the Spring, which is surrounded by jagged [[Ice]] formations. It is a shallow pool of [[Water (Terrain)|Water]] that flows into two small [[Waterfall]]s at either side of its entrance. There is a [[Goddess Statue]] at its center known as the [[Spring of Wisdom Statue]], where [[Link]] can exchange four [[Spirit Orb]]s for either [[Heart Container]]s or [[Stamina Vessel]]s.<ref>{{Cite|It appears you have claimed {{Color BotW|Red|four}} {{Color BotW|Blue|Spirit Orbs}}. In exchange for {{Color BotW|Red|four}} {{Color BotW|Blue|Spirit Orbs}}, I will amplify your being. So tell me what it is that you desire.|Spring of Wisdom Statue|BotW}}</ref> Due to being within a [[Freezing Climate]], Link will take damage at the Spring of Wisdom unless he has two levels of [[Cold Resistance]]. Since ancient times, the [[Dragon]], [[Naydra]], has served the Spring.<ref>{{Cite|A spirit of ice has taken the form of this giant dragon. Making its home in the Lanayru region, it's said to have served the Spring of Wisdom since ancient times. An old saying goes, "The dragon ascends to the heavens as the sun begins to set," but nobody has seen this in the current age. The ice that coats its body makes it dangerous to get near, but Naydra bears no ill will toward people.|Hyrule Compendium|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite Book|quote= |book= CaC |publisher= |page= 158}}</ref>

Prior to the second [[Great Calamity]], the Spring of Wisdom was the final spring that [[Princess Zelda|Zelda]] visited, since those under the age of 17 are not wise enough to climb Mount Lanayru.<ref>{{Cite|See that mountain? That's Mt. Lanayru. It takes its name from the Goddess of Wisdom. Lanayru's decree is very specific. It says: "No one is allowed, under the age of seventeen... For only the wise are permitted a place upon the mountain." I've prayed at the Spring of Courage and at the Spring of Power, yet neither awoke anything inside me. But maybe up there... Perhaps the Spring of Wisdom, the final of the three, will be the one.|Princess Zelda|BotW}}</ref><ref name="CaC 379">{{Cite Book|quote= |book= CaC |publisher= |page= 379}}</ref> On the day of her 17th birthday, Zelda visited the Spring of Wisdom.<ref name="CaC 379"/><ref>{{Cite|Tomorrow...is my seventeenth birthday. So then I shall go...and make my way up the mountain.|Princess Zelda|BotW}}</ref> However, she failed to awaken her sealing power, and she and Link can be seen returning from this journey during the "[[Return of Calamity Ganon]]" [[Recovered Memory]].<ref name="CaC 379"/><ref>{{Cite|So you didn't feel anything? No power at all?|Revali|BotW}}<br/>{{Cite|I'm sorry, no.|Princess Zelda|BotW}}</ref>

In [[Hateno Village]], Link can ask [[Medda]] about Mount Lanayru, who believes that the [[Royal Family of Hyrule]] could have a hidden treasure at the Spring of Wisdom.<ref>{{Cite|Yeah, {{Color BotW|Blue|Mount Lanayru}}'s interesting... The {{Color BotW|Red|Spring of Wisdom}} the princess of {{Color BotW|Blue|Hyrule}} used for the purification is said to be somewhere on that mountain. A special fountain? That the princess had to endure hardship to visit? I bet the royal family left a treasure there! ...Well, at least maybe they could've. I would've if I was a royal.|Medda|BotW}}</ref> After listening to him, "[[The Spring of Wisdom]]" [[Shrine Quest]] will begin. When Link first arrives at the Spring of Wisdom, he will find [[Malice Naydra]], a form of Naydra after she has been corrupted by [[Malice]]. [[Hylia]] speaks to him through the Spring of Wisdom Statue, revealing that she has been afflicted by an attack from [[Calamity Ganon]].<ref>{{Cite|You have done well to find your way to this spring. You who have overcome numerous trials and obtained the {{Color BotW|Blue|Spirit Orbs}}... The one you see before you is an attendant to the {{Color BotW|Blue|Spring of Wisdom}}. This is {{Color BotW|Blue|Naydra}}, the blue spirit of Lanayru. This servant of the Goddess has looked over the spirits of this land for ages, unknown to the world of man. However, the dreaded Malice unleashed by Calamity Ganon has possessed its body and reduced it to this state.|Spring of Wisdom Statue|BotW}}</ref> She tasks Link with destroying the [[Glowing Eyeball]]s and freeing Naydra.<ref>{{Cite|You who have received the Spirit Orbs... Free {{Color BotW|Blue|Naydra}} from this Malice. Show what your power can achieve!|Spring of Wisdom Statue|BotW}}</ref> After Link shoots one of the Glowing Eyeballs on Malice Naydra, she will fly away from the Spring of Wisdom.

Once Naydra has been purified, Link will automatically return to the Spring of Wisdom. As a final task, Hylia instructs Link to shoot Naydra with an [[Arrow]].<ref>{{Cite|Thanks to your efforts, {{Color BotW|Blue|Naydra}}, the spirit of Mount Lanayru, has been freed from the grips of an {{Color BotW|Red|evil power}}. But a single ceremony remains. Now... Loose your arrow through the body of {{Color BotW|Blue|Naydra}} to free the spirit of this region!|Spring of Wisdom Statue|BotW}}</ref> When he does so, Naydra will fly off, but not before dropping one of her [[Naydra's Scale|Scales]] to the ground.<ref>{{Cite|When {{Color BotW|Red|Naydra}} soared away into the heavens, it left behind {{Color BotW|Red|Naydra's scale}}.|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|That is the spirit {{Color BotW|Blue|Naydra's scale}}. It fell when your arrow struck. It serves as proof of the courage you received from the one who served the spring since ancient times.|Spring of Wisdom Statue|BotW}}</ref> Link is then told to offer Naydra's Scale to the Spring of Wisdom.<ref>{{Cite|Come... Offer a {{Color BotW|Blue|scale}} from the blue spirit {{Color BotW|Blue|Naydra}} to the {{Color BotW|Blue|Spring of Wisdom}}.|Spring of Wisdom Statue|BotW}}</ref> Doing this will open the door to [[Jitan Sa'mi Shrine]] behind the Statue.<ref>{{Cite|Your path has shown itself. Now go forth.|Spring of Wisdom Statue|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|When you tossed {{Color BotW|Red|Naydra's scale}} into the Spring of Wisdom, an ancient shrine appeared.|Adventure Log|BotW}}</ref>

After being freed, Naydra will appear above the Spring of Wisdom at 5:00 AM and 5:00 PM everyday. However, she will not do so if Link is at the Spring during these times.

